# %% [markdown]
# # DriftSense — 04: Expected-Cost Forecasting & Conformal Calibration (v2)
#
# **Runtime Type:** Python 3 (CPU or GPU)  
# **Estimated Runtime:** ~1-3 minutes  
# **RAM Needed:** ~2-4 GB  
# **Disk Needed:** ~1 GB  
# **Expected Outputs:**  
# - Model Checkpoints: `runs/<run_id>/models/{seasonal_naive,moving_average,ets,sarima,boosted_tree,quantile}.joblib`  
# - Conformal Prediction Intervals: `runs/<run_id>/val_conformal_intervals.csv`  
# - Validation Metrics Report: `runs/<run_id>/val_forecast_metrics_v2.json`  
# - Validation Predictions Matrix: `runs/<run_id>/val_forecast_predictions_v2.csv`  
# - Comparative Forecast & Conformal Band Visualization: `runs/<run_id>/forecast_comparison_v2.png`  
# - Cryptographically Verified Manifest: `runs/<run_id>/manifest.json`  
#
# > **CRITICAL EVALUATION & ISOLATION INVARIANTS (Rule C3, C6, C7):**  
# > - **Holdout Quarantine:** The holdout test partition ($D_{\text{test}}$) is strictly quarantined and touched by ZERO forecasters or calibrators. Model evaluation occurs exclusively on validation ($D_{\text{val}}$). Manifest records `holdout_touched=false`.  
# > - **Scale-Independent Metric Selection:** Evaluated via **WAPE**, **sMAPE**, **MASE**, and **masked MAPE** to handle zero-inflation and sparsity.  
# > - **Finite-Sample Uncertainty:** Split-conformal calibration on validation residuals guarantees marginal interval coverage $1 - \alpha$.

